<article class="env-lemma" id="06YT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06YT">Lemma <span data-tag="06YT">21.17.12</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. Let $\alpha : \mathcal{P}^\bullet \to \mathcal{Q}^\bullet $ be a quasi-isomorphism of K-flat complexes of $\mathcal{O}$-modules. For every complex $\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ of $\mathcal{O}$-modules the induced map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Tot}(\text{id}_{\mathcal{F}^\bullet } \otimes \alpha ) : \text{Tot}(\mathcal{F}^\bullet \otimes _\mathcal {O} \mathcal{P}^\bullet ) \longrightarrow \text{Tot}(\mathcal{F}^\bullet \otimes _\mathcal {O} \mathcal{Q}^\bullet )  \]
</div>
  <p> is a quasi-isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a quasi-isomorphism $\mathcal{K}^\bullet \to \mathcal{F}^\bullet $ with $\mathcal{K}^\bullet $ a K-flat complex, see Lemma <a href="/tag/06YS" data-tag="06YS">21.17.11</a>. Consider the commutative diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \text{Tot}(\mathcal{K}^\bullet \otimes _\mathcal {O} \mathcal{P}^\bullet ) \ar[r] \ar[d] &  \text{Tot}(\mathcal{K}^\bullet \otimes _\mathcal {O} \mathcal{Q}^\bullet ) \ar[d] \\  \text{Tot}(\mathcal{F}^\bullet \otimes _\mathcal {O} \mathcal{P}^\bullet ) \ar[r] &  \text{Tot}(\mathcal{F}^\bullet \otimes _\mathcal {O} \mathcal{Q}^\bullet ) }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       The result follows as by Lemma <a href="/tag/06YP" data-tag="06YP">21.17.3</a> the vertical arrows and the top horizontal arrow are quasi-isomorphisms. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>